arr=np.array(Image.open(logo).convert('RGB'));m=(arr[:,:,0]>220)&(arr[:,:,1]>220)&(arr[:,:,2]>220)
y=np.arange(410,611);x=np.array([np.where(m[yy])[0].min() for yy in y]);slope,intercept=np.polyfit(y,x,1);angle=math.degrees(math.atan(abs(slope)));dx=round(1080*abs(slope))
(g/'geometry.json').write_text(json.dumps({'method':'leftmost white pixel per scanline, y410..610, threshold R/G/B>220; least-squares x versus y','slope_dx_per_dy':float(slope),'angle_off_vertical_degrees':angle,'canvas_1080_delta_x':dx,'logo_sha256':hashlib.sha256(logo.read_bytes()).hexdigest()},indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
(g/'ART_DIRECTION.md').write_text(f'''# Direction decision - before implementation

A - Decision cut. Strategic idea: reveal a decision and the evidence it needs. One diagonal boundary uses the original V's measured {angle:.2f} degree lean; two fields carry question and rule, orange marks the decision once. Asymmetrical Arabic-first headings, Cairo 900/700 with calm Latin support; white clarifies method, navy groups evidence. Imagery remains truthful and licensed; diagrams labelled CONCEPT, not proof. Risks: cuts can become ornament; require one meaningful relationship and one focal point.

B - Scope ledger. Strategic idea: make scope visible as an editorial register. Vertical ledger columns, numbered rules, tabulated evidence, no diagonal split. Cairo 700, disciplined baseline, alternating navy and white; orange indexes records. Calm detail imagery after rights verified. Risk: usable but resembles any architecture documentation system and loses the distinctive logo's direction.

Select A: geometry can survive removal of colour/logo, links to the user's approved direction and supports question-to-detail-to-rule. Reject B as the primary device; retain tabular discipline only when needed for rules. Native applications adapt cut scale and information order; never simply resize.

Palette is approved; execution and LENS verbal are draft for review. No fabricated plan/built/QC records. SK-008 direction method; SK-002 rule structure; SK-005 AR-first role scale; SK-010 actual render inspection.
''',encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
